/-!
# Structurality from `Equation4408` through a two-guard companion

Generated by `defwork/itautcell2.py`.  `Equation4408` is `x ◇ (x ◇ y) = (y ◇ y) ◇ x`.  Its guarded obligation
-- a bijection of a finite model commuting with `x □ y = if (M.op a a) = b then (M.op a b) else if (M.op b b) = a then b else (M.op a b)` is an automorphism of `◇` --
is `GuardAut2_pxx_y_pyy_x_pxy_y_pxy_Equation4408`, proved elsewhere.  That obligation names no target, so every
law the companion satisfies is another cell for free, and there
are 2 of them below.
-/

open FirstOrder FirstOrder.Language Law Law.MagmaLaw FreeMagma

set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000
